        'nodes' => array(
            '5.7' => implode("\n", array(
                'Safety Performance Monitoring and Measurement',
                '',
                'Safety performance monitoring and measurement is the process by which EuroPilot Center’s safety performance is verified against the overall safety policy and objectives.',
                '',
                'Safety performance is the level of safety achievement against the Safety Performance Objectives (SPOs), using specific Safety Performance Indicators (SPIs). Safety performance reflects the ability of EuroPilot Center to manage risk effectively.',
            )),
            '5.7.1' => implode("\n", array(
                'Stepwise Approach to Safety Performance Measurement',
                '',
                'At different levels of SMS maturity, the amount and quality of available safety data, and the issues and actions most important for improving safety performance, will differ. EuroPilot Center therefore applies a stepwise approach based on three levels of SMS maturity.',
                '',
                'LEVEL 1 — Present and Suitable',
                '',
                'At Level 1, the SMS has achieved compliance with the applicable requirements. SPIs focus on the activities required to maintain basic compliance with the SMS regulatory framework and may be quantitative or qualitative.',
                '',
                'Quantitative indicators may include:',
                '• the number of safety reviews performed;',
                '• the number of personnel who received SMS training; and',
                '• the number of internal audits performed compared with the number planned.',
                '',
                'Qualitative indicators may include:',
                '• feedback from personnel on the safety policy; and',
                '• feedback from personnel on new procedures for internal occurrence reporting or hazard identification.',
                '',
                'Once the SMS is established and compliance has been achieved, Level 2 indicators shall be introduced to support improvement of safety performance.',
                '',
                'LEVEL 2 — Operating and Effective',
                '',
                'At Level 2, EuroPilot Center defines more specific SPIs using safety data collected through hazard-identification and internal occurrence-reporting processes. More specific, objective and reliable leading indicators and precursor-event indicators are used to identify weaknesses and areas requiring improvement. These may include:',
                '• the number of risk assessments performed following organizational changes;',
                '• the percentage of standard operating procedures subjected to hazard identification;',
                '• average lead time for completing corrective actions following internal audit; and',
                '• the number of additional procedural controls implemented.',
                '',
                'At this level of maturity, EuroPilot Center develops a clearer picture of the risks affecting its operations and the strength of the risk controls in place.',
                '',
                'LEVEL 3 — Best Practice',
                '',
                'At Level 3, EuroPilot Center has achieved continuous learning and improvement throughout the SMS. Effective hazard-identification and risk-assessment processes support a more sophisticated mix of SPIs. SPIs focus on local issues identified from collected safety data and on key safety areas identified by the competent authority or the aviation sector.',
                '',
                'SPIs allow monitoring of occurrence-related risk levels, the strength of safety barriers and their relationship to accidents. Risk-mitigation actions focus on issues presenting the greatest risk or greatest opportunity for improvement.',
                '',
                'Quantitative indicators may include:',
                '• the number of high-risk occurrences classified amber or red;',
                '• the mean value of risk ratings over a defined reference period;',
                '• the sum of risk ratings over a defined reference period; and',
                '• the strength of risk controls or defences, rated over a defined reference period.',
                '',
                'Following implementation of risk-mitigation actions, risks shall be monitored to verify that the controls are effective and to identify how the controls may be improved.',
            )),
            '5.7.2' => implode("\n", array(
                'Setting Safety Performance Objectives',
                '',
                'The process for determining quantitative safety-performance objectives for a defined period consists of:',
                '1. measuring the baseline against which safety improvements will be assessed;',
                '2. setting reasonable but appropriately ambitious targets; and',
                '3. monitoring achievement over time and reviewing targets as necessary.',
                '',
                'The Safety Manager shall ensure that SPOs and SPIs are pertinent and documented.',
            )),
            '5.7.3' => implode("\n", array(
                'Process',
                '',
                'The Safety Manager shall ensure that the safety-performance measurement process is established and implemented. SPOs shall be monitored over time by the Safety Manager and reviewed by the Safety Review Board, or by the Accountable Manager together with the Safety Manager. SPIs shall also be reviewed following implementation of a change. A report shall be provided annually to the Safety Review Board and the Accountable Manager.',
                '',
                'The safety-performance monitoring and measurement process includes the following:',
                '',
                'A. Safety Reporting',
                '',
                'The Safety Manager collects and centralizes EuroPilot Center safety reports and monitors the type and number of reported events over time. The Safety Manager also monitors compliance with the applicable requirements.',
                '',
                'In addition, the safety-performance monitoring process shall use controlled information from Section 5.6, including occurrence categories, reportability outcomes, initial and follow-up authority-reporting performance, investigation findings, open and overdue actions, residual-risk acceptances, effectiveness outcomes, escalation status and closure performance. Aggregate monitoring shall identify trends and systemic issues without replacing accountable follow-up of individual occurrences under Section 5.6.',
                '',
                'B. Safety Studies',
                '',
                'Safety studies are detailed analyses used to address broad safety concerns. The Safety Manager shall initiate safety studies when appropriate on subjects relevant to EuroPilot Center.',
                '',
                'Safety studies gather additional information on selected topics identified through safety reports or other means. They are broader in scope than the analysis of a specific hazard and may include safety surveys.',
                '',
                'Safety studies may address subjects such as compliance with Standard Operating Procedures, mission preparation, or the risk assessment of specific operations, including deteriorating weather or external pressure.',
                '',
                'Safety studies may use information published by manufacturers, original equipment manufacturers, competent authorities, aviation associations, national or international safety initiatives, technical journals, accident and incident reports, conference proceedings, press releases and other reliable safety sources.',
                '',
                'Safety studies shall be retained as controlled records in the Safety Study Folder.',
                '',
                'C. Safety Reviews',
                '',
                'Safety reviews, including trend reviews, shall be conducted during the introduction and deployment of new technologies, changes to or implementation of procedures, and structural changes to operations.',
                '',
                'A safety review shall be performed at least annually by the Safety Review Board or by the Safety Manager and Accountable Manager.',
                '',
                'The safety review shall assess:',
                '• safety performance against the safety indicators and objectives;',
                '• the effectiveness of the Safety Management System, including the effect of corrective or preventive actions;',
                '• procedures and policies; and',
                '• occupational health and safety matters.',
                '',
                'Negative trends and deficiencies may be identified and actions taken to address their causes. Corrective actions shall be recorded. The model in OMM Annex 9 — Corrective Action Follow-up may be used.',
                '',
                'D. Safety Audits',
                '',
                'Safety audits focus on the integrity of the management system and periodically assess the status of safety-risk controls. The audit schedule is contained in Annex 12 — Safety Audit Schedule.',
                '',
                'EuroPilot Center shall address audit findings through appropriate corrective action to restore or improve the effectiveness of the SMS and safety performance. The model in OMM Annex 9 — Corrective Action Follow-up may be used.',
                '',
                'The Safety Manager is responsible for internal safety audits but may be assisted by another internal or external auditor.',
                '',
                'E. Safety Surveys',
                '',
                'Safety surveys are qualitative or quantitative studies directed at specific safety subjects. They may be used to evaluate elements or procedures of an operation, including daily operational problem areas, perceptions, opinions, satisfaction levels and areas of disagreement or uncertainty, and to collect comments and suggestions.',
            )),
